{"id": "EUVD-2026-106921", "enisaUuid": "0b6115a6-62b6-3b74-9df0-6d4311e9c3d2", "description": "Vyper 0.3.4 through 0.5.0b1 computes the remaining blueprint size in create_from_blueprint by uint256 subtraction without first checking that code_offset is below the blueprint's code size, so a huge offset wraps to a small positive value. An attacker controlling code_offset can make a factory deploy contracts with no runtime code, potentially trapping ETH and tokens.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:37:15", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/security/advisories/GHSA-fxg7-4wqg-c8gh", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vyper-0.3.4-through-0.5-0b1-create-from-blueprint-offset-validation-bypass-via-unsigned-wraparound"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p4mc-qjvf-mf2m", "CVE-2026-114118"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "564a56b0-e0cf-31cc-a1aa-a15630cadec8", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0.3.4 \u22640.5.0b1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "06a2ca0c-96ac-3efe-aab9-39c85e4e88a4", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}], "isExploited": false}